  "id": "Compound::DB00738 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Pentamidine exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c19 and Cyp1a2, which are both involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. This binding leads to the participation of these enzymes in the epoxygenation and monooxygenation of arachidonic acid, respectively. These enzymatic activities ultimately result in the participation of Cyp2d6, suggesting a potential mechanistic link between Pentamidine and Cyp2d6. The evidence is supported by a consistent pattern of interaction across three distinct paths, with similar scores indicating a reliable relationship. The shared involvement of Cyp2d6 in the metabolism of arachidonic acid suggests that Pentamidine may modulate Cyp2d6 activity through a common pathway, potentially affecting lipid metabolism or inflammatory processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Cyp2d6 in the metabolic conversion of arachidonic acid, and the binding of Pentamidine may influence this process through a shared enzymatic activity.",
